# Deny-by-default build context.
#
# Two images are built from this context and they need different things:
#
#   Dockerfile     the CLI *runtime* — copies only src/starsky/ and the builder's
#                  .venv, so nothing else in the context can reach it
#   Containerfile  the *tools* image — needs site/ (package.json + bun.lock) to
#                  install the frontend dependencies
#
# Because the runtime image copies a fixed allowlist, permitting site/ here for
# the tools build cannot leak the site into production. Keeping only files that
# are neither secrets nor junk in the context is what this file is for.

# VCS and local state — never.
.git/
.github/
.devcontainer/
.gitignore
.env*
!.env.example

# Build outputs and installed dependencies — always rebuilt.
dist/
node_modules/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
build/
.pytest_cache/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# The sky-data cache is generated, not source.
site/public/data/*.json

# Documentation: not needed by either build. README stays for image labels.
*.md
!README.md

# Permitted: everything the two Dockerfiles mount or copy, i.e. the Python
# package + manifests, and the site's manifests for the tools install.
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!src/**
!site/package.json
!site/bun.lock
!site/tsconfig.json
!Containerfile
!Dockerfile
